# knowledge.p0t — convertito da tests/knowledge.sh (gen444).
#
# gen151: the gen150 expert/skill knowledge must be SPOKEN, not dumped as raw
# Prolog. These tests query the domain knowledge conversationally and assert a
# natural sentence — proving the description facts verbalize through one general
# path (no per-concept phrasebook) and that no clause leaks as "pred(arg, ...)".
# EN + IT exercise the SAME render path, the bilingual ratchet (LOOP.md step 6).

[test knowledge]
!set PARROT0_BASE=kb/core/base.p0
!set PARROT0_SESSION=
!set PARROT0_PROFILE=kb/experts/mathematics/arithmetic.p0
!reset

# arithmetic: what is addition
> what is addition
< addition is combining two numbers to get their sum.

# arithmetic: bare concept (no article)
> what is prime
< prime is a number greater than 1 divisible only by 1 and itself.
[test knowledge_1]
!set PARROT0_BASE=kb/core/base.p0
!set PARROT0_SESSION=
!set PARROT0_PROFILE=kb/experts/medicine/anatomy.p0
!reset

# anatomy: what is the heart
> what is the heart
< heart is muscular pump circulating blood through the body.

# anatomy: what is the femur
> what is the femur
< femur is thigh bone -- longest and strongest bone in the body.

# anatomy: tell me about the brain
> tell me about the brain
< brain is control center processing sensory information and directing responses.
[test knowledge_2]
!set PARROT0_BASE=kb/core/base.p0
!set PARROT0_SESSION=
!set PARROT0_PROFILE=kb/profiles/agi.p0
!reset

# long+comma description (was mangled): kiss
> what is kiss
< kiss is keep it simple, stupid — prefer simple, obvious solutions over clever ones.

# long description (was dropped): api
> what is api
< api is Application Programming Interface — a set of functions for building software.
[test knowledge_3]
!set PARROT0_BASE=kb/core/base.p0
!set PARROT0_SESSION=
!set PARROT0_PROFILE=kb/experts/mathematics/arithmetic.p0
!reset

# IT: cos'e addition
> cos'è addition
< addition is combining two numbers to get their sum.

# IT: cos'e multiplication
> cos'è multiplication
< multiplication is repeated addition of a number.
[test knowledge_4]
!set PARROT0_BASE=kb/core/base.p0
!set PARROT0_SESSION=
!set PARROT0_PROFILE=kb/experts/medicine/anatomy.p0
!reset

# recall by property (held-out): longest bone -> femur
> what is the longest bone in the body
< You might mean femur: thigh bone -- longest and strongest bone in the body.
[test knowledge_5]
!set PARROT0_BASE=kb/core/base.p0
!set PARROT0_SESSION=
!set PARROT0_PROFILE=kb/experts/mathematics/arithmetic.p0
!reset

# recall by paraphrase (held-out): combines two numbers -> addition
> what is the operation that combines two numbers
< You might mean addition: combining two numbers to get their sum.

# IT cross-lingual cognate recall: -> pi
> qual è il rapporto tra circonferenza e diametro
< You might mean pi: 3.14159... -- the ratio of a circle's circumference to its diameter.
[test knowledge_6]
!set PARROT0_BASE=kb/core/base.p0
!set PARROT0_SESSION=
!set PARROT0_PROFILE=kb/profiles/agi.p0
!reset

# idf breaks agi-scale tie: pumps blood -> heart
> what is the organ that pumps blood
< You might mean heart: muscular pump circulating blood through the body.
[test knowledge_7]
!set PARROT0_BASE=kb/core/base.p0
!set PARROT0_SESSION=
!set PARROT0_PROFILE=kb/experts/medicine/anatomy.p0
!reset

# emergent containment: heart -> circulatory
> what is the heart part of
< heart is part of circulatory: heart and blood vessels -- transports blood, oxygen and nutrients.

# emergent containment: liver -> digestive
> what system is the liver part of
< liver is part of digestive: stomach, intestines and liver -- breaks down and absorbs food.

# IT emergent containment: di cosa fa parte heart
> di cosa fa parte heart
< heart is part of circulatory: heart and blood vessels -- transports blood, oxygen and nutrients.

# no fabricated relation: femur is unplaced
> what is the femur part of
< I don't understand that yet.

# prove derived relation: heart in circulatory
> is the heart part of the circulatory system
< Yes, heart is part of circulatory.

# disprove (honest): heart not in digestive
> is the heart part of the digestive system
< No, I have no evidence that heart is part of digestive.

# inverse query: members of the digestive system
> what is part of the digestive system
< digestive contains: stomach, intestines, liver.

# type gate: a system is not part of a sibling system
> is skeletal part of muscular
< No, I have no evidence that skeletal is part of muscular.

# honest miss: unknown topic does not fuzzy-fire
> what is the weather like today
< I don't understand that yet.
